# .worktreeinclude — gitignored local state auto-copied into each new worktree at creation
# (Claude Code feature; .gitignore syntax; only files that match a pattern AND are gitignored
# are copied, so tracked files are never duplicated). This gives a fresh worktree the untracked
# fixtures it needs, plus a warm start for both test environments.
#
# The ROOT Manifest.toml is deliberately absent from the list below (#624). Copying it
# propagated the main checkout's pre-#34 manifest — which still lists LibPQ/SQLite as hard
# `[deps]` — into every worktree, and since `Pkg.instantiate()` only warns about a stale
# manifest instead of re-resolving it, that made the package-env spelling of the unit suite
# look green everywhere until the first re-resolve silently dropped both. Let instantiate resolve
# the truth instead; it is seconds against an already-populated depot.
#
# test/integration/Manifest.toml IS copied: that environment lists both drivers in `[deps]`,
# so its manifest is correct rather than a survival, and the copy is a genuine warm start.
#
# NOT listed on purpose:
#   - test/integration/db_2/migrations  — TRACKED (already present in every worktree).
#   - test/integration/db_sl/f1.sqlite  — 42 MB + torn-WAL risk on unconditional copy; copied
#                                          on demand (guarded) by scripts/worktree_setup.sh,
#                                          needed only for db_sl integration runs.
#
# Still run after creation: `bash scripts/worktree_setup.sh`, which instantiates BOTH the
# package env and test/integration (instantiate is not a file copy, so .worktreeinclude
# cannot do it) and copies the guarded f1.sqlite.

test/integration/Manifest.toml
test/integration/db_sl/connection.yml
test/integration/db_2/connection.yml
test/integration/db_sl/migrations/
